@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "license"

Feature: License
	Testing general license features.

Teardown:
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I tear down the contacts from the account "Liferay.com" on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| license.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| license.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| license.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| license.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
 	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| license.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| license.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: Generate developer license as employee
	New Liferay employees should be able to generate a developer license.

	Given I wait for "5" seconds
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | license.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | license.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | License                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                            |
	And I assign the web user with the email address "license.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to the web organization "Liferay, Inc."
	And I assign the web user with the email address "license.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to the web role "Verified User"
	Then the support user with the email address "license.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	When I assign the support user with the email address "license.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "license.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to the support group "Guest"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "license.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to the support role "Liferay Employee"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "license.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to the support user group "liferay employee"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "license.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I assign worker contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Liferay.com"
	| license.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "license.employee1@liferay.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the License Management page
	And I click on the Generate New License button
	And I generate a new license with the following values
	| Default Account        | Liferay.com                                | |
	| Product                | DXP Development                            | |
	| Choose Liferay Version | 7.2                                        | |
	| Type                   | Digital Enterprise Development (Developer) | |
	| Choose Purchase        | Detached                                   | |
	And I go to the License Management page
	And I search the License Management page with the account key value "KOR-86488333"
	Then I should be able to view the license with the name "Liferay.com" following values
	| Project         | LIFERAY.COM         |
	| Name            | Liferay.com         |
	| Product         | DXP Development 7.2 |
	| Type            | Developer           |